 "capsule": "The state of Song (宋) was created after the Zhou conquest of Shang (c. 1046 BCE) as an enclave at Shangqiu granted to the defeated Shang royal house, first under Weizi, so that Shang ancestral rites could continue. Nominally honored for its royal pedigree, Song nonetheless fought as an ordinary Zhou-era power through the Spring and Autumn and Warring States periods, and tradition traces Confucius's ancestry to its ducal line. Song was destroyed in 286 BCE when Qi, aided by Chu and Wei, partitioned its territory following the excesses of its last ruler, King Kang.",
